I have created the following custom SQL function on a PostgreSQL 16.1 server to generate a series of monthly dates between two given dates:
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.generate_series_monthly(a date, b date)
RETURNS SETOF date LANGUAGE SQL IMMUTABLE PARALLEL SAFE ROWS 12 AS $function$
select generate_series(date_trunc('month', a), date_trunc('month', b), '1 month')
$function$;
Specifically, I have added the row estimate parameter, and as expected, I am seeing this estimate in some simple queries:
explain select generate_series_monthly('2023-01-01', '2023-12-01');
However, in some uses in queries, I see it falling back to the default of 1000:
explain select * from generate_series_monthly('2023-01-01', '2023-12-01');
I would expect this second query to also use the 12 row estimate. Why is it resorting to 1000?

